1
00:00:02,000 --> 00:00:05,357
Mind the rocks, Tom! The
tide's coming in fast.

2
00:00:05,957 --> 00:00:09,386
I can see something in the
water. Is that a man?

3
00:00:09,986 --> 00:00:11,914
Father! Father, come quick!

4
00:00:12,514 --> 00:00:15,729
What is it now, boy? I've
only just sat down.

5
00:00:16,329 --> 00:00:19,829
There's a man in the water,
near the black rocks.

6
00:00:20,429 --> 00:00:23,429
Bloody hell. Fetch the rope from the shed.

7
00:00:24,029 --> 00:00:27,671
Mrs. Penrose, put the kettle
on, we've got company.

8
00:00:28,271 --> 00:00:30,629
Lord have mercy. Is he breathing?

9
00:00:31,229 --> 00:00:33,371
Barely. Help me turn him over.

10
00:00:33,971 --> 00:00:36,471
He's ice cold. Get him by the fire.

11
00:00:37,071 --> 00:00:39,500
Who are you, sir? Can you hear me?

12
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:42,171
Water... Where... where am I?

13
00:00:42,771 --> 00:00:46,343
You're at the Godrevy light,
sir. You're safe now.

14
00:00:46,943 --> 00:00:49,800
Godrevy? No. No, I must get to Falmouth.

15
00:00:50,400 --> 00:00:54,186
You'll not get anywhere
tonight, not in this weather.

16
00:00:54,786 --> 00:00:57,857
Is he a smuggler? He looks
like a smuggler.

17
00:00:58,457 --> 00:01:01,600
Hush, Ellen. Don't be rude
to the gentleman.

18
00:01:02,200 --> 00:01:04,914
I'm not being rude. I'm being careful.

19
00:01:05,514 --> 00:01:08,443
She's right to be careful, Mr. Trevaskis.

20
00:01:09,043 --> 00:01:10,757
How do you know my name?

21
00:01:11,357 --> 00:01:15,000
It's sewn into your coat. "J.
Trevaskis, Penzance."

22
00:01:15,600 --> 00:01:18,600
Then you've read more of me than I'd like.

23
00:01:19,200 --> 00:01:22,557
Drink this. It's brandy.
It'll warm your bones.

24
00:01:23,157 --> 00:01:25,657
Thank you, madam. You're very kind.

25
00:01:26,257 --> 00:01:28,471
Kind? I'm only kind on Sundays.

26
00:01:29,071 --> 00:01:31,714
Today's Tuesday. Then you're in luck.

27
00:01:32,314 --> 00:01:35,314
Tom, go and light the lamp. It's past six.

28
00:01:35,914 --> 00:01:39,486
Can't Helen do it? I'm always
the one who goes up.

29
00:01:40,086 --> 00:01:43,514
Because Ellen lit it
yesterday, and you know it.

30
00:01:44,114 --> 00:01:47,186
Fine. But I'm not cleaning
the glass after.

31
00:01:47,786 --> 00:01:51,214
You'll clean the glass, or
you'll get no supper.

32
00:01:51,814 --> 00:01:54,529
That's not fair! Life's not fair, boy.

33
00:01:55,129 --> 00:01:58,414
Ask the poor sod on the
rocks if life is fair.

34
00:01:59,014 --> 00:02:02,229
The others... were there
others in the water?

35
00:02:02,829 --> 00:02:05,257
We saw no one else, sir. Only you.

36
00:02:05,857 --> 00:02:08,643
There were three of us on the Maryanne.

37
00:02:09,243 --> 00:02:12,529
Captain Boase and his son.
The boy was twelve.

38
00:02:13,129 --> 00:02:16,271
I'm sorry, sir. The sea
takes what it wants.

39
00:02:16,871 --> 00:02:19,871
Don't say that, Mrs. Penrose. Not tonight.

40
00:02:20,471 --> 00:02:23,186
Forgive me. I didn't mean it unkindly.

41
00:02:23,786 --> 00:02:26,500
What were you carrying, Mr. Trevaskis?

42
00:02:27,100 --> 00:02:30,100
Tin. Only tin, from the mine at Botallack.

43
00:02:30,700 --> 00:02:33,271
Tin don't sink a boat in calm water.

44
00:02:33,871 --> 00:02:36,157
It wasn't calm. You saw the sky.

45
00:02:36,757 --> 00:02:39,686
I saw the sky, aye. And I saw your hands.

46
00:02:40,286 --> 00:02:42,143
My hands? What about them?

47
00:02:42,743 --> 00:02:46,243
Those aren't a sailor's
hands. Too clean by half.

48
00:02:46,843 --> 00:02:49,129
Father, stop it. He's half dead.

49
00:02:49,729 --> 00:02:52,371
Half dead men tell whole lies, Ellen.

50
00:02:52,971 --> 00:02:56,257
I'm a clerk. I keep the
books for the company.

51
00:02:56,857 --> 00:02:59,714
Then why was a clerk on a boat at night?

52
00:03:00,314 --> 00:03:03,743
Because the company asked me
to count something.

53
00:03:04,343 --> 00:03:07,057
Count what? Count what, Mr. Trevaskis?

54
00:03:07,657 --> 00:03:10,800
Money, Mr. Penrose. Money
that went missing.

55
00:03:11,400 --> 00:03:12,900
Oh, Lord. Here we go.

56
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:16,071
The lamp's lit! Did I miss anything?

57
00:03:16,671 --> 00:03:19,457
Only everything. Sit down and be quiet.

58
00:03:20,057 --> 00:03:22,129
How much money? A great deal.

59
00:03:22,729 --> 00:03:25,729
Enough to make a man drown another for it?

60
00:03:26,329 --> 00:03:28,471
Enough to make a man do worse.

61
00:03:29,071 --> 00:03:31,714
Then we'd best lock the door tonight.

62
00:03:32,314 --> 00:03:35,314
Tom, bring the shotgun down from the loft.

63
00:03:35,914 --> 00:03:38,486
Is it loaded? It was last Christmas.

64
00:03:39,086 --> 00:03:42,514
That's not funny, Father. It
wasn't meant to be.

65
00:03:43,114 --> 00:03:46,329
Someone's coming up the
path. With a lantern.

66
00:03:46,929 --> 00:03:50,357
At this hour? Nobody comes up
here at this hour.

67
00:03:50,957 --> 00:03:53,671
Get back from the window, both of you.

68
00:03:54,271 --> 00:03:56,986
Penrose! Open up! It's the coastguard!

69
00:03:57,586 --> 00:04:00,800
That's not the coastguard.
I know that voice.

70
00:04:01,400 --> 00:04:03,614
Who is it, then? Captain Boase.

71
00:04:04,214 --> 00:04:07,714
But you said he drowned. I
said I didn't see him.

72
00:04:08,314 --> 00:04:10,029
I never said he drowned.

73
00:04:10,629 --> 00:04:13,914
Open the door, Penrose, or
I'll break it down!

74
00:04:14,514 --> 00:04:17,443
You'll do no such thing, not in my house!

75
00:04:18,043 --> 00:04:20,971
Mrs. Penrose, take the children upstairs.

76
00:04:21,571 --> 00:04:23,643
I'm not a child! I'm fifteen!

77
00:04:24,243 --> 00:04:25,957
Then act like it and go.

78
00:04:26,557 --> 00:04:30,700
Mr. Trevaskis, is there anything
else you haven't told us?

79
00:04:31,300 --> 00:04:33,657
Only that the money's in my boot.

80
00:04:34,257 --> 00:04:35,457
Well, bugger me.

